DeltaVR License Information
===========================

The DeltaVR project uses a split-licensing model to protect our team's 
hand-written documentation, custom hardware designs, and tracking software. 
By accessing, modifying, or distributing any part of this project, you 
agree to the terms of the respective licenses below.

1. SOFTWARE, FIRMWARE & SIMULATION WORK
---------------------------------------
All custom source code, firmware, tracking algorithms, and simulation scripts
(including everything within the /software/ and /deltavirtual/ directories) 
are licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0). 
See the full text in LICENSE-SOFTWARE.txt.

* NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY TOOLS: Third-party simulation binaries or testing tools 
  included within these directories (such as Renode or its dependencies) 
  remain under their own respective open-source licenses as provided by 
  their original authors. Our license applies strictly to the custom 
  simulation files, setups, and scripts authored by the DeltaVR team.

2. HARDWARE & PCB DESIGN LICENSE
--------------------------------
All custom hardware schematics, PCB layouts, bill of materials (BOM), 3D 
printable models, and compiled manufacturing bundles (including everything 
located within the /kicad/, /bom/, /pcb files for jlcpcb/, and /release v1.0.0/ 
directories) are licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - 
Strongly Reciprocal (CERN-OHL-S v2). See the full text in LICENSE-HARDWARE.txt.

3. HANDWRITTEN DOCUMENTATION & KNOWLEDGE BASES
----------------------------------------------
All project documentation, wiring guides, design previews, and hand-written 
notes (including everything located within the /docs/, /logos/, and 
/obsidian files/ directories) are licensed under a Creative Commons 
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0).
